  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A small wooded canyon with a stream running through it, lined with impressive 80-metre-high red cliffs that recall Corsica and have earned the gorges the nickname "Colorado of the Estérel" in Bagnols-en-Forêt, in the Pays de Fayence. The site is also a major climbing spot (more than 450 equipped routes according to the tourist offices), with the Colle Rousse sector for beginners. Along the way you pass the Grotte du Muéron, inhabited in the Bronze Age, remains of 18th-century millstones, cork oaks, chestnut trees and wild orchids.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>For the walk, the tourist office recommends the Gorges du Blavet car park (at the bottom), on the D47 from Bagnols-en-Forêt towards La Motte and Draguignan, where several shaded tables are set up. The loop described by Visit Var is 6.5 km with 204 m of ascent, with two fords across the Blavet, a bridge over rock potholes and a return via the Bayonne track; the Pays de Fayence office estimates 2h30 and judges it not very difficult, whereas Visit Var rates it red level, difficult. Both sources agree on one point: the waymarking is hard to see in places, and the circuit should be avoided in rainy weather. According to the tourist office, there is no water in the gorges in summer, even though the undergrowth stays cool: this is not a swimming spot, and you need to bring water for your dog.</p>
      <p>The circuit is in the Estérel massif, whose access is regulated in summer by the prefecture: check the day's map from June to September. No source read publishes a dog rule for this site: keep yours close, especially at the fords and around the cliffs where climbers are active. The view from the viewpoint indicator (with a picnic table), at the roadside on the D47, covers the sea to the south, the hills to the north, the Estérel massif and the Roquebrune rock; the viewpoint car park is at the roadside, with a risk of scraping for a low vehicle. Leave nothing of value in the car.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: pair this outing with the nearby Gorges de la Siagne and de la Siagnole for a full day in the area.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The hilltop villages of Fayence, Callian or Montauroux are charming for extending the day. Information: Pays de Fayence inter-municipal tourist office, 04 94 76 01 02.</p>
